          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Moore complex
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            – also known in its normalized version as the
            %strong complex of normalized chains
            – is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            is built from the face maps of the simplicial group.
          %p
            The operation of forming the Moore complex of chains of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            is one part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            that relates
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            (abelian)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                whose
                = succeed "-cells" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "-disks" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                the boundary map on which acts literally like a boundary map should: it sends an
                = succeed "-disk" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "-disk" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %p
            This is entirely analogous to how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            is obtained from a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} strict ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            in the section on the nonabelian version.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ForGeneralSimplicialGroups For general simplicial groups
          #NormalizedChainComplexOnGeneralGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complex"} normalized chain complex
              or
              %em Moore complex
              is the
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((N G)_\bullet,\partial )
              of (possibly
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"} nonabelian
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  is in degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  the joint
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %munderover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %mi ker
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msubsup
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (N G)_n=\bigcap_{i=1}^{n}ker\,d_i^n
                %p of all face maps except the 0-face;
              %li
                %p with differential given by the remaining 0-face map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≔
                        %msubsup
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                          %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi N
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\partial_n \coloneqq d_0^n|_{(N G)_n} : (N G)_n \rightarrow (N G)_{n-1}
                        \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalizedChainComplexOnGeneralGroup"}
              one may equivalently take the joint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of all but the
              = succeed "-face" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n^n
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              We may think of the elements of the complex
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N G
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalizedChainComplexOnGeneralGroup"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              as being
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disks"} disks
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              all of whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              is captured by a single face:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in N G_1
                  in degree 1 is a 1-disk
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi g
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi g
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        1 \stackrel{g}{\to} \partial g
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  an element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in N G_2
                  is a 2-disk
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ⇓
                                  %mi h
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %mi h
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mn 1
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; 1
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^1\nearrow &amp;\Downarrow^h&amp; \searrow^{\partial h}
                        \\\
                        1
                        \&amp;&amp;\stackrel{1}{\to}&amp;&amp;
                        1
                        }
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  a degree 2 element in the kernel of the boundary map is such a 2-disk that is closed to a 2-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ⇓
                                  %mi h
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %mi h
                                    %mo =
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mn 1
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; 1
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^1\nearrow &amp;\Downarrow^h&amp; \searrow^{\partial h = 1}
                        \\\
                        1
                        \&amp;&amp;\stackrel{1}{\to}&amp;&amp;
                        1
                        }
                        \\,,
            %p etc.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              the normalized chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N G)_\bullet
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalizedChainComplexOnGeneralGroup"}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+complex+of+groups"} normal complex of groups
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p This means that is easy to take the homology of the complex, even though the groups involved may be non-abelian.
          %h3#ForSimplicialAbelianGroups For simplicial abelian groups
          %p
            Let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+group"} simplicial abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complex"} normalized chain complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (N A)_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet^+
            of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalizedChainComplexOnGeneralGroup"}
            is an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+chain+complex"} connective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
          %p
            In this abelian cases are two other chain complexes naturally associated with
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          #AlternatingFaceMapComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+group"} simplicial abelian group
              its
              %strong alternating face map complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C A)_\bullet
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              which
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  in degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  is given by the group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
                  itself
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (C A)_n \coloneqq A_n
              %li
                %p
                  with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
                  given by the alternating sum of face maps (using the abelian group structure on
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                #eq:DifferentialOnChains.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≔
                        %munderover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\partial_n \coloneqq \sum_{i = 0}^n (-1)^i d_i  \;\colon\; (C A)_n \to (C A)_{n-1}
                        \\,.
                %p
                  (see lemma
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlternatingSumOfFacesInNilpotent"}
          #AlternatingSumOfFacesInNilpotent.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The differential in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlternatingFaceMapComplex"}
              is well-defined in that it indeed squares to 0.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i \circ d_j = d_{j-1} \circ d_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \lt j
              one finds:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
